From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: csid: leave the IFE core clock rate to the VFE

On SoCs where the CSID sits inside the IFE, the CSID resources list the
IFE core clock ("vfeN", "vfe_lite") with its rate table, and
csid_set_clock_rates() sets every clock that is not a "csiN" clock to
its first rate. That clobbers the rate the VFE chose for the pipeline:
the CSID powers its parent VFE, which sizes the IFE clock, then knocks it
back to the lowest level, and when the pipeline powers the VFE itself
vfe_check_clock_rates() finds it too low and fails with -EBUSY.

On SM8350 an IMX563 at 4121.6 Mpix/s needs the IFE at 720 MHz, so every
stream failed with "Failed to power up pipeline: -16". Leave the IFE
core clock rate to the VFE. Sensors that fit the lowest level are
unaffected: their colour bars are byte-identical before and after.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c |   13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c
index 90d28e5..d35d80f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c
@@ -536,6 +536,17 @@ const struct csid_format_info *csid_get_fmt_entry(const struct csid_format_info
  * csid_set_clock_rates - Calculate and set clock rates on CSID module
  * @csiphy: CSID device
  */
+/*
+ * The IFE core clock in a CSID's clock list ("vfeN", "vfe_lite"): on SoCs
+ * where the CSID sits inside the IFE the CSID needs it running, but the VFE
+ * owns its rate and sizes it for the pipeline in vfe_set_clock_rates().
+ */
+static bool csid_is_ife_core_clock(const struct camss_clock *clock)
+{
+	return !strcmp(clock->name, "vfe_lite") ||
+	       (!strncmp(clock->name, "vfe", 3) && !strchr(clock->name, '_'));
+}
+
 static int csid_set_clock_rates(struct csid_device *csid)
 {
 	struct device *dev = csid->camss->dev;
@@ -592,7 +603,7 @@ static int csid_set_clock_rates(struct csid_device *csid)
 				dev_err(dev, "clk set rate failed: %d\n", ret);
 				return ret;
 			}
-		} else if (clock->nfreqs) {
+		} else if (clock->nfreqs && !csid_is_ife_core_clock(clock)) {
 			clk_set_rate(clock->clk, clock->freq[0]);
 		}
 	}
